---
import PrivacyLayout from "../../components/PrivacyLayout.astro";
---

<PrivacyLayout
    title="Privacy Policy - PinoBlu"
    appName="PinoBlu"
    lastUpdated="16 October 2026"
    accentColor="#3498db"
>
    <div class="my-5 rounded-md border-l-4 border-emerald-500/80 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <strong>In summary:</strong> PinoBlu is an online multiplayer game. It has no
        account system, does not ask for your email or any personal details, and the
        only information you provide is a nickname you choose yourself. The game
        contains no advertising, analytics, or third-party tracking services.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        PinoBlu is a multiplayer game developed by Mariano Riefolo and distributed
        for Android through Google Play. Playing online connects your device to a
        game server operated by the developer at
        <code>wss://pinoblu.rfmariano.it</code>. This policy explains what data the
        game and that server handle, and how.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data you provide</h2>
    <p>
        PinoBlu does not require an account, registration, login, email address, or
        password. The only piece of personal data you give the game is a
        <strong>nickname</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            You choose it yourself in the game. It is limited to 1–16 printable
            characters and defaults to "Pino" if you do not change it.
        </li>
        <li>
            It is saved on your device and sent to the game server only when you play
            online, so other players and the leaderboard can identify you.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Please do not enter your real name or any other personal information as your
        nickname, because it is visible to other players and may be published on
        public leaderboards.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
        PinoBlu keeps a single local save file in the app's private storage
        (<code>save.json</code>, inside the PinoBlu data folder). It contains only
        game data:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your best score for each difficulty</li>
        <li>Your in-game coins and unlocked skins and backgrounds</li>
        <li>Audio, display, and gameplay preferences</li>
        <li>Your chosen nickname</li>
        <li>Short match receipts used to avoid awarding the same result twice</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This file lives inside the app's private storage and is not readable by other
        apps under normal operating conditions. The game does not store any
        credentials, passwords, or authentication tokens on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Network communications</h2>
    <p>
        When you play online, the game opens a single encrypted connection (WebSocket
        over TLS) to the developer's game server at
        <code>wss://pinoblu.rfmariano.it/ws</code>. Over that connection the game
        sends only what is needed to run the match:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your nickname</li>
        <li>A random value generated fresh for each connection (not a device identifier)</li>
        <li>A platform code identifying the game engine build</li>
        <li>Your movement input during a match</li>
        <li>Matchmaking preferences such as difficulty, skin, and background</li>
        <li>The room code when you join a private room</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The game does not send your name, email, phone number, contacts, location,
        device identifiers, advertising ID, or any hardware or operating-system
        information.
    </p>
    <p>
        As with any online service, the game server can see the IP address your device
        connects from in order to route traffic and protect against abuse (for
        example, anti-spoofing checks). The server uses the IP address only
        transiently for this purpose and does not store or log it.
    </p>

    <h2>5. The game server, other players, and leaderboards</h2>
    <p>
        The game server is authoritative, meaning it runs the match, and is operated
        by the developer. It keeps the following in memory while you are connected,
        and discards it when you leave or when the server restarts:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your session, nickname, platform, and preferences</li>
        <li>Your match state and in-progress scores</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        When you play with others, the players in your lobby can see your nickname and
        the skin and background you chose. In addition, the server keeps a
        <strong>public solo leaderboard</strong>: your best score for each difficulty,
        together with your nickname, is stored on the server and shown to any player
        who opens the leaderboard. This leaderboard is the only information that
        persists after you disconnect.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data we do not collect</h2>
    <p>PinoBlu does not collect, transmit, share, or sell:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Names, email addresses, phone numbers, or postal addresses</li>
        <li>Account credentials or passwords (there is no account system)</li>
        <li>Device identifiers, advertising IDs, or hardware or OS information</li>
        <li>Location data</li>
        <li>Contacts, photos, files, camera, or microphone data</li>
        <li>App usage analytics, behavioral profiling, or crash reports</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. App permissions</h2>
    <p>PinoBlu requests only two Android permissions:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Internet access:</strong> required to connect to the game server
            for online play
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Network state:</strong> to detect connectivity so the game can
            handle going online or offline
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The game does not request access to contacts, location, camera, microphone,
        storage, phone state, or any other sensitive permissions. Single-player modes
        work without any network connection.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Advertising, analytics, and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
        PinoBlu contains no advertising SDKs, analytics services, crash-reporting
        services, social media SDKs, or other tracking technologies, and the game
        server shares no data with third parties. No third party receives data from
        the game.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you obtain PinoBlu through Google Play, Google may independently process
        information related to store access, downloads, installation, and device
        services. This processing is performed by Google, not by PinoBlu, and is
        governed by the
        <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80"
        >Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
        Data on your device, including your save file and nickname, stays until you
        change it, clear the app's storage through Android settings, or uninstall the
        app. Uninstalling removes all local data.
    </p>
    <p>
        Online match data is temporary and is discarded when you disconnect or when
        the server restarts. Leaderboard entries, however, persist on the server.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Your control over your data</h2>
    <p>Because PinoBlu has no account, you are always in control:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Change:</strong> pick a different nickname at any time in the game
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Delete locally:</strong> clear the app's storage or uninstall the
            app to remove all on-device data
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
        PinoBlu does not knowingly collect personal information from children. The
        game has no account system and asks for no personal details beyond a
        self-chosen nickname. If you believe a child has provided personal information
        through the game, please contact us and we will remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
        This policy may be updated if PinoBlu's features or data-handling practices
        change. The current version and its latest revision date will always be
        published on this page. Material changes may also be communicated through an
        app update or its Google Play listing.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Regulatory compliance</h2>
    <p>PinoBlu is designed to comply with:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>CCPA (California Consumer Privacy Act)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Other applicable privacy regulations</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="my-5 rounded-md border-l-4 border-emerald-500/80 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <strong>Remember:</strong> PinoBlu has no account and collects no personal
        details. The only information you provide is a nickname you choose, which may
        be shown to other players and published on public leaderboards.
    </div>
</PrivacyLayout>
